  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "nOpGLy0WeJ4+I3Ln/XYuvab+Ymk=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T14:34:03.469Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Every mutation in the reactor is processed as a **job**, and the job \u2014 not the action \u2014 is the unit whose progress you can observe. Jobs move through:\n\n```\nPENDING -> RUNNING -> WRITE_READY -> READ_READY\n                   \\-> FAILED\n```\n\n- `PENDING` \u2014 queued, not yet started.\n- `RUNNING` \u2014 the reducer is executing.\n- `WRITE_READY` \u2014 operations have been written to the operation store.\n- `READ_READY` \u2014 all read models have finished processing; the document is fully readable.\n- `FAILED` \u2014 an unrecoverable error.\n\nOnly `READ_READY` and `FAILED` are terminal. `WRITE_READY` is the subtle one: the operation is durably persisted at that point, but the read models have not caught up, so a read issued immediately may not see the change. That gap is exactly what the extra hop to `READ_READY` closes.\n\nThis is why the two client entry points behave so differently. `IReactorClient.execute()` waits until the job reaches `READ_READY` before resolving \u2014 you get read-after-write consistency, at the cost of blocking through the read-model phase. `executeAsync()` returns immediately with a `JobInfo` still at `PENDING`; you then either poll `getJobStatus(jobId)` or await `waitForJob(job.id)`.\n\n```typescript\nconst job = await reactorClient.executeAsync(docId, \"main\", actions);\nconst completed = await reactorClient.waitForJob(job.id);\n```\n\nThe distinction matters for anything that writes on a hot path. Processors, for instance, must use their `dispatch` handle (which wraps `executeAsync`) rather than a blocking `execute()`, because a processor that waits for `READ_READY` can block on the very pipeline it is part of.\n\nThe status enum is mirrored by the event bus: `JOB_PENDING` (10001), `JOB_RUNNING` (10002), `JOB_WRITE_READY` (10003), `JOB_READ_READY` (10004), `JOB_FAILED` (10005).\n\n_Source: apps/academy/docs/academy/04-Reference/01-Reactor/01-WorkingWithTheReactor.md (Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45)._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-13T14:34:02.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T14:34:03.469Z"
    }
  },
